Excluded, with reasons: Marie Dubois (Sorbonne has only 6 current students — 8 of the 14 enrolled in Math201 graduated before 2025-08-16), John Smith (MIT, no EU department), Athanasios Voulodimos and Stefan Mueller (assistant professors). Current-enrollment counts: ComputerScience_NTUA 12, HistoryAndPhilosophy_NKUA 12, Engineering_Berkeley 11, Biology_MIT 7, Mathematics_Sorbonne 6.

## Verification

No SPARQL engine was available and the sandbox has no network (`rdflib`/`pip` absent, `curl` blocked by policy), so I parsed the Turtle and evaluated the query clause-by-clause in Python, twice with independently written checkers. Both reproduced the 3 rows above. The checkers also assert against the file on disk: all 21 expected graph patterns present, the `IN` list is exactly the EU-27 (no `CH`, no `US`, no omissions), and the reference date `2025-08-16` is used. Throwaway scripts were deleted, leaving only `solution.sparql`.

Two data quirks worth knowing: `Student5` references an undefined `uni:Bio10` (it joins nothing, so it silently contributes no enrollment — it does not affect any count here), and the file uses CRLF line endings.

